2026-09-10T09:08:20.493307+00:00 critic on 2f995f47d421807a: keep=False issues=["No evidence anywhere associates 'shor-bell-labs' (Peter Shor) with blackbody-spectrum quantization or with 1913; Shor's known work (in the broader corpus context) is 1990s quantum algorithms, decades after 1913, and blackbody quantization belongs to Planck (1900), not to the named actor."]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493320+00:00 critic on 659cb0f0b0dbc50c: keep=False issues=["No evidence places 'ibm-quantum' at the 1930 Solvay Conference in Brussels; all IBM-related evidence in the corpus (DiVincenzo 2000, IBM Quantum Experience 2016, IBM Q System One 2019, Eagle 2021, etc.) dates IBM's quantum activity to 2000 onward, decades after 1930."]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493334+00:00 critic on 9b695beeeb84af4d: keep=False issues=["No evidence places 'ibm-quantum' at CERN in the 1950s or has it 'proving' matrix-wave-mechanics; all IBM-quantum evidence dates from 2000 onward, and matrix-wave-mechanics (Heisenberg/Schrödinger) is dated 1925-1926 in the evidence, not the 1950s."]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493347+00:00 critic on 26ed76417ca76643: keep=True issues=[]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493360+00:00 critic on d08adda270589f47: keep=False issues=["Refuting evidence T-foundations-ms-3 dates Bell's theorem/Bell-CERN activity to 1964, not 1924; John Bell was not born until 1928, making any 1924 activity by this actor impossible per the evidence timeline."]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493375+00:00 critic on 53aaf6b3040a93c8: keep=False issues=["Place 'bell-labs-nj' is anachronistic for the interval [1916,1919]: Bell Labs was not founded until 1925, so it cannot have hosted any actor or event in 1916–1919.", 'No evidence anywhere connects Bohr (or the cited Sommerfeld quantization work) to Bell Labs; the only supporting item naming the interval attributes the work to Sommerfeld, not Bohr taking any action there.']
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493390+00:00 critic on 2da0eb6f517eda84: keep=False issues=['The named actor (Hanson group/Hensen/Bernien et al., TU Delft) is attested in the evidence only for a 2015 experiment (T-belltests-ms-0); nothing places this actor or its members active in 1900.', 'The 1900 blackbody-spectrum quantization episode (Planck) belongs to a different actor entirely; the evidence set contains no link between the named 2015-era experimental group and any 1900 event.']
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493403+00:00 critic on e49520792029e45b: keep=True issues=[]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493478+00:00 critic on 56592a9248038ba6: keep=False issues=['BB84 is attested (T-qinfobirth-ms-5) as a 1984 protocol by Bennett & Brassard, not Bohr, and not in 1916–1919 — the object did not exist for roughly 65 years after the stated interval.', 'No evidence connects Bohr to BB84 at any time.']
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493551+00:00 critic on f15b8d459226827f: keep=True issues=[]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493595+00:00 critic on f4fbb850d8c4a0aa: keep=False issues=["CERN was not founded until 1954, making 'cern' an impossible place for a 1930 event.", 'No evidence places Einstein at CERN at any time.']
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493627+00:00 critic on f16253658083537a: keep=True issues=[]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493658+00:00 critic on 148b734b7711b19a: keep=True issues=[]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493692+00:00 critic on e8e67eb910713403: keep=False issues=["Interval [1927,1927] contradicts the evidenced timeline for Shor's algorithm: the refuting evidence dates the direct algorithmic precursor (Simon's problem) to 1994 and the whole quantum-computing lineage (Benioff's model) to 1980 at the earliest, so 'shors-algorithm' cannot be placed in 1927, decades before quantum computing as a field existed.", "Mechanism 'wave-particle-duality' has no evidenced connection to Shor's algorithm, which is a computational/number-theoretic result (period-finding), not a wave-particle-duality phenomenon."]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493737+00:00 critic on 4e22e2dfecb38e4f: keep=False issues=["Interval [1927,1927] contradicts the evidenced Bell-inequality/Bell-test timeline, which the evidence dates from Aspect's 1981-82 experiments through 2015-2018 loophole-closing tests — decades after 1927, and Bell's theorem itself (1964) postdates even EPR (1935), which the object presupposes.", "Place 'bell-labs-nj' is contradicted by the located Bell-test evidence, which places the relevant experiments at Orsay, Vienna, NIST Boulder, and via cosmic-photon sources — never Bell Labs NJ."]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493777+00:00 critic on 1b728a8202824e1c: keep=True issues=[]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493811+00:00 critic on aea977a3a3d5b910: keep=False issues=["Place 'berkeley' directly contradicts the supporting evidence, which explicitly locates the drafting/formalization of matrix mechanics on Helgoland and in Göttingen (Born, Heisenberg, Jordan) — no Berkeley connection appears anywhere in the record.", "Interval [1925,1925] mismatches half the actor pair: Schrödinger's wave mechanics is dated by the evidence to 1926 (Annalen der Physik four-part series), not 1925."]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493846+00:00 critic on 7d50af53ee0289f2: keep=False issues=["Interval [1910,1919] places the quantum-error-correction threshold theorem seven decades before the evidenced birth of quantum computing itself (Benioff 1980 is the earliest cited quantum-computing precursor), making the object's existence in that window impossible per the record.", "Mechanism 'quantum-error-correction' and object 'threshold-theorem' presuppose a computational quantum-information framework that the evidence shows did not exist until the 1970s-1990s (Holevo 1973, Wiesner ~1970, Benioff 1980, Simon 1994) at the earliest."]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493879+00:00 critic on a337b83045ec6db0: keep=False issues=["Actor 'heisenberg-schrodinger' is contradicted by the supporting evidence itself, which attributes the EPR paper and the associated 1935 debate explicitly to Einstein ('Einstein shifts ground...the EPR paper' and 'EPR is a valid argument'), not to Heisenberg or Schrödinger as the paper's authors."]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493913+00:00 critic on 6fd0d29023b018e9: keep=False issues=["Place 'ibm-yorktown' sits outside every tradition Einstein belonged to in 1935: the evidenced EPR/Solvay-era record places Einstein's 1935 activity in the Princeton context (Phys. Rev. 47, 777, 1935), and IBM's Yorktown research site is a mid-20th-century (1961+) institution with no evidenced connection to Einstein's 1935 work."]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493946+00:00 critic on edc7816f52e5dc19: keep=False issues=["Actor 'google-quantum-ai' is not attested within the stated 1913 time bin: the evidence's entire quantum-computing/quantum-technology company timeline (D-Wave 2011, Atom Computing 2023, Quantinuum 2025) places such actors exclusively in the 2010s-2020s, and blackbody-spectrum quantization (Planck-era physics) predates any quantum-computing organization by roughly a century."]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.493976+00:00 critic on fe13e7c8ad072ca8: keep=True issues=[]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.494007+00:00 critic on 8841f6ccab435315: keep=False issues=["place='cern' contradicts the cited T1 evidence, which states Bell wrote the 1964 theorem 'on sabbatical from CERN' — i.e., while away from CERN, not at CERN."]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.494040+00:00 critic on 3a241a55ab7a5717: keep=False issues=["object='sycamore-supremacy-claim' cannot fall in interval [1960,1969]: T-birth-ms-0/T-birth-ms-1 (T1) establish 1980 as the earliest published suggestion of quantum computation (Manin; Benioff), decades after the stated interval, and quantum supremacy claims (Sycamore) postdate even that by ~39 years."]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.494072+00:00 critic on 1eafec343bdd787b: keep=False issues=["object='sycamore-supremacy-claim' cannot fall in interval [1950,1959]: T-birth-ms-1 (T1) establishes 1980 as the earliest quantum-computation concept, decades after this interval.", "actor='planck' with action='factored' on a quantum-computing supremacy claim has no support and is contradicted by the same 1980-earliest-concept evidence establishing the object could not exist in the 1950s."]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.494111+00:00 critic on 8f489cfe255a7663: keep=False issues=["actor='aspect-clauser-zeilinger' is tied by T-nobel-claim-1 (T1) to the 2022 Nobel Prize for Bell-test experiments, not to any 1924 activity; no evidence attests this actor group active in 1924.", "object='matrix-wave-mechanics' is anachronistic for 1924: the supporting evidence (T-old-ms-7) is specifically about de Broglie's 1924 matter-wave thesis, not matrix or wave mechanics, which per the broader record only emerge in 1925–1926."]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.494148+00:00 critic on 4c442773174bf7e7: keep=False issues=["mechanism='decoherence' at interval=[1927,1927] contradicts T-foundations-ms-6 (T1), which states the decoherence program began in 1970 (Zeh) — decoherence as a named mechanism did not exist in 1927."]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.494177+00:00 critic on 493857e09c167540: keep=True issues=[]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.494209+00:00 critic on 9a7dffd043c0cc13: keep=False issues=["actor='uu-eu-quantum-flagship' is explicitly dated to 2016 by T-2ndrev-ms-4 and T-race-ms-5 (T5), not 1900, directly contradicting the stated interval=[1900,1900]."]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.494241+00:00 critic on 3f56e9cd4f9f260e: keep=True issues=["No evidence attests to Einstein 'factoring' anything, or to any 'other-object' at Solvay — action/object fields are unsupported placeholders, not contradicted", 'Interval end-year 2009 corresponds only to the Bacciagaluppi & Valentini publication date, not an event date, but this is not a contradiction of the 1927 Solvay placement']
2026-09-10T09:08:20.494273+00:00 critic on e89af63312c028dc: keep=False issues=["T-formalism-ms-8 states Einstein's 1935 EPR paper 'defined the question Bell made testable 29 years later,' i.e. Bell's inequality dates to ~1964, not 1935 — directly contradicts pairing object='bell-inequality' with interval=[1935,1935]"]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.494305+00:00 critic on c947b6b89c151581: keep=True issues=["mechanism='entanglement' is not evidenced for Einstein's 1905–1926 quantization work (T-old-ms-1, T-old-ms-6); this is unsupported rather than contradicted", "object='other-object' and place='other-place' are generic and not tied to any specific counter-evidence"]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.494337+00:00 critic on 7982a6227a72b8f5: keep=True issues=['No evidence in the supporting or refuting sets mentions Bohr, a 1913 event, or blackbody-spectrum at all — the hypothesis is entirely unsupported by the given corpus', "action='factored' has no attestation anywhere for Bohr"]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.494369+00:00 critic on 6288d1adaa60bf15: keep=False issues=['No-cloning theorem is dated to 1982 by T-birth-ms-3 and T-qinfobirth-ms-3, directly contradicting the stated interval [1920,1929]', "'vendor-marketing' as actor proving a physics/CS theorem is not attested by any source; the theorem is attributed to Wootters & Zurek / Dieks"]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.494422+00:00 critic on 56db9ec75836a01c: keep=False issues=['No-cloning theorem is dated to 1982 by T-birth-ms-3 and T-qinfobirth-ms-3, directly contradicting the stated interval [1930,1939]', 'The theorem is attributed to Wootters & Zurek / Dieks, not Planck, in every piece of evidence that mentions it']
2026-09-10T09:08:20.494462+00:00 critic on 985b07167e6e2926: keep=True issues=["No evidence in the corpus mentions a 'threshold-theorem' at all, so the object field is entirely unsupported", "action='other-action' and mechanism='other-mechanism' are generic placeholders with no specific attestation"]
2026-09-10T09:08:20.494495+00:00 critic on 90831130b6c48a83: keep=True issues=["T-old-ms-3 credits the 1916–1919 Bohr–Sommerfeld quantization scheme primarily to Sommerfeld, not solely to Bohr, so Bohr's individual authorship in this exact window is only implied by the compound name, not stated outright"]
